WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:18.140
This video describes how to prepare the child and mother or carer before performing the fundal red reflex tests in both newborns and older children.

2
00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:29.140
The child should be held securely yet comfortably, either on the lap, over a shoulder, or, if a baby, lying on their back.

3
00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:37.120
It is important for them to feel safe. Young babies can be restless and may need to be swaddled.

4
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:44.180
Examining shortly after a feed can help as they will be relaxed and a little sleepy.

5
00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:49.220
Older children may settle by playing with a toy for a short while.

6
00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:55.320
Speak with a friendly tone and try to get down to their eye level.

7
00:00:55.320 --> 00:01:00.500
Explain what you are going to do and gain consent before you start.

8
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:10.440
First, ask the mother or carer if they have seen anything wrong with their child's eye or vision and how long they have noticed the problem.

9
00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:15.120
Next, look at the child's face and eyes. Ask yourself some questions.

10
00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:24.300
Does the child seem to have pain in one or both eyes? Are the eyes open or are they keeping them tightly shut?

11
00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:31.280
Is there watering or discharge from the eyes? Are the eyes the same size? Are the eyelids swollen?

12
00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:38.580
Now, consider how the child is seeing. Move your face slowly from side to side, watching their eyes.

13
00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:47.970
Make some silent smiles. Does the child follow the movement of your face or respond to your silent smile?

14
00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:53.990
Again, ask yourself some questions. Do both eyes move freely and together?

15
00:01:54.430 --> 00:02:01.110
Are the eyes straight or is one eye turning inwards or outwards? Do the eyes wobble?

16
00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:12.200
You can also use the lights on the Arclight and picture targets to gain attention and assess the quality of vision.

17
00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:20.660
Move the target side to side, up and down. Look to see if the child is fixing and following the target.

18
00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:26.600
Can they reach and point accurately at the target?

19
00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:35.060
Often, only one eye cannot see well. You or the mother can cover one eye, then the other.

20
00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:43.320
Move the target and compare how the child behaves to when using both eyes, then one at a time.

21
00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:51.380
If the child does not like one eye being covered, it suggests the uncovered eye does not see so well.

22
00:02:51.560 --> 00:03:00.560
If you think you can see something wrong with the external eye, look more closely using the loupe end of the Arclight.

23
00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:12.150
Switch the lights on and move up close to around 6 cm. You may need to use your finger to gently open the eyelids.

24
00:03:12.890 --> 00:03:24.070
Ask yourself some questions. Is the white part of the eye pink or red? Is the pupil or cornea grey or white?

25
00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:35.160
Is the pupil round? Can you see any foreign bodies? Now you are ready to perform the reflex tests.

